The six scans are English pages but were processed with the Tamil OCR model, producing the mixed-script source preserved verbatim. They were re-OCR'd locally with the English model. Obvious OCR substitutions, broken line-end hyphenation, punctuation and a few grammatical artefacts were normalised conservatively in the recovered transcription. The file contains three distinct Assembly interventions under one date; all three are retained. "Lord Earl Home" in the OCR is rendered as "Lord Home," the historical title used by Alec Douglas-Home, while the verbatim OCR remains unchanged above.
